        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="EfcTNxSgW_AFl3pymhPJ-95" edge="1" parent="1" style="shape=flexArrow;endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;" target="EfcTNxSgW_AFl3pymhPJ-96" value="">
          <mxGeometry height="50" relative="1" width="50" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="-925" y="261" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="-855" y="91" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="EfcTNxSgW_AFl3pymhPJ-96" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;autosizeText=1;fontColor=#000000;darkOpacity=0.05;fillColor=#FFF9B2;strokeColor=none;fillStyle=solid;fontSize=11;direction=west;gradientDirection=north;gradientColor=#FFF2A1;shadow=1;size=20;pointerEvents=1;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;Validating that it holds to 2.3% across a 16× range, and the counterintuitive practical consequence — larger deltas merge more faithfully, so scaling up α improves absorption. Most people assume bigger perturbations round worse. That&#39;s a real, actionable calibration.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;What would upgrade it to 🚀: a measured deviation from the theoretical constant that survives scrutiny and points at a mechanism. Right now the data agrees with the one-line prediction.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;Storing W+dW in bf16 perturbs it by ≈ε·‖W‖ regardless of dW (since dW ≪ W). That error, expressed relative to ‖dW‖, is ε·‖W‖/‖dW‖ = ε / (‖dW‖/‖W‖).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="190" width="310" x="-1275" y="-11" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="EfcTNxSgW_AFl3pymhPJ-99" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;autosizeText=1;darkOpacity=0.05;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;fillStyle=solid;fontSize=18;direction=west;gradientDirection=north;shadow=1;size=20;pointerEvents=1;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;⭐ restore write&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
